Photorealistic style: A weathered stone bridge spanning a deep chasm, with one half of the bridge constructed from ancient, crumbling Roman stonework covered in moss and vines, while the other half transitions seamlessly into sleek modern steel and glass architecture. The two halves meet in the middle where cracks are visible and small pieces are falling into the misty void below. Golden hour lighting casts long shadows across the structure, emphasizing the tension between old and new. A single figure stands at the junction point, looking down at the fracture lines, their silhouette small against the massive engineering challenge. Storm clouds gather on the horizon behind the old section while clear blue sky opens above the modern portion. The perspective is from slightly below, looking up at the bridge's underside where support structures from different eras intertwine awkwardly.
